        {
          "source_quote": "τὰς πάντων φορτισθεὶς φροντίδας",
          "english_quote": "having taken upon yourself the cares of everyone",
          "issue": "The passive participle explicitly depicts Clement as loaded or burdened with everyone's cares. The draft shifts the grammatical agency and makes the burden image less explicit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “burdened with the cares of everyone.” This proposed replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τὸ σὲ οἰκονομεῖν ἀναδέξασθαι χάριν οἶδα εἰληφώς, οὐ δεδωκώς",
          "english_quote": "Hence I know that, in your undertaking to administer, I have received a favor, not given one.",
          "issue": "The infinitival construction leaves the assignment of subject and object unresolved. The notes disclose Clement undertaking administration and the speaker undertaking to have Clement administer, but do not separately examine σέ as the object of οἰκονομεῖν, with the speaker undertaking to direct or make provision for Clement. These analyses materially affect the account of who undertakes what. The independently image-checked print establishes the supplied wording, not the preferred syntactic interpretation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Supply separate grammatical and contextual evidence comparing these analyses of the exact Lagarde reading. Expand source_issues to include the object analysis and preserve the uncertainty until adjudicated. If a different reading is proposed, identify its textual evidence separately rather than silently replacing the supplied Greek. Any revised English requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "17",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "checks": {
