    {
      "reference": "18",
      "verdict": "blocked",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": true,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ἵνα ἕκαστος, ἐπιδικαζόμενος τοῦ πάντας φίλους ἔχειν, αὐτὸν διαλλάττων σώζηται",
          "english_quote": "so that each person, pressing his claim to have everyone as friends, may be saved by reconciling him",
          "issue": "The draft preserves the pronoun and discloses uncertainty, but the referent of αὐτόν and the relationship expressed by διαλλάττων remain unresolved. Reconciling the presiding leader, reconciling an alienated person, and effecting reconciliation with the referent are materially different interpretations. Disclosure does not resolve this blocking meaning problem.",
          "suggested_revision": "Provide separate contextual and grammatical evidence identifying the likely referent and the construction of active διαλλάττων with αὐτόν. Retain the supplied wording and unresolved alternatives meanwhile. The print transcription is already image-checked; this finding does not establish textual corruption. Any more explicit English must undergo fresh review.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τῆς αὐτοῦ ἐπακούων ὁμιλίας",
          "english_quote": "and heeding his discourse",
          "issue": "The antecedent of αὐτοῦ remains unresolved. Connecting it with the presiding leader rather than another participant in the preceding reconciliation clause changes whose discourse is to be heeded. The existing note honestly discloses this problem but supplies no separate evidence settling it.",
          "suggested_revision": "Provide an independently supported contextual account of the pronoun sequence, coordinated with the analysis of αὐτὸν διαλλάττων. Preserve the neutral pronoun and the unresolved source_issues until that evidence is reviewed; do not certify a particular antecedent merely because the English remains ambiguous.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "19",
      "verdict": "blocked",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἀξιῶ σε ἐπὶ πάντων μου τῶν συνπαρόντων ἀδελφῶν, ὅπως ὁπόταν τοῦ ἐνταῦθα (ὡς ἐμοὶ ὀφείλεται) ἀπαλλάξω βίου, σὲ Ἰακώβῳ τῷ ἀδελφῷ τοῦ κυρίου διαπέμψαι ἐν ἐπιτομῇ ἀναγραψάμενον μέχρι καὶ τῶν ἐκ παίδων σου λογισμῶν καὶ ὡς ἀπ᾽ ἀρχῆς μέχρι τοῦ νῦν συνώδευσάς μοι, ἐπακούων τῶν κατὰ πόλιν ὑπ᾽ ἐμοῦ κηρυχθέντων λόγων τε καὶ πράξεων, ἔπειτα πρὸς τῷ τέλει καὶ τὴν τοῦ θανάτου μου πρόφασιν ὡς προεῖπον δηλῶσαι μὴ ὀκνήσῃς",
          "english_quote": "Before all my brothers who are here with me, I charge you: whenever I depart from this life here—as is owed to me—send James, the Lord’s brother, a concise written account, reaching back even to your thoughts from childhood and telling how, from the beginning until now, you have traveled with me, listening to the words and deeds proclaimed by me from city to city. Then, toward the end, do not hesitate also to make known the cause of my death, as I foretold.",
          "issue": "The extended construction remains unresolved. The draft attaches “do not hesitate” explicitly only to disclosure of the death's cause. A substantial alternative takes the concluding μὴ ὀκνήσῃς as governing both διαπέμψαι and δηλῶσαι within the request introduced by ὅπως. The function of the resumed σέ and its relationship to ἀναγραψάμενον also require analysis. The existing note acknowledges these difficulties but does not settle the chosen English structure.",
          "suggested_revision": "Supply separate grammatical evidence for the relationships among Ἀξιῶ σε, ὅπως, the resumed σέ, both infinitives, and μὴ ὀκνήσῃς. Explicitly compare the current English with a construction beginning “I ask you … not to hesitate to send … and then, toward the end, also to make known …”. Do not adopt that proposal without fresh review. Preserve the supplied Greek; unusual syntax and the image-checked punctuation do not themselves establish corruption.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "οὐκ ἀμαθὴς ἀνὴρ καὶ ζωοποιοὺς λόγους ἀγνοῶν καὶ ἐκκλησίας κανόνα. οὐκ εἰδὼς τὴν τοῦ διδάσκοντος ἐπιστεύθη καθέδραν",
          "english_quote": "after me the teacher’s chair was not entrusted to an unlearned man who is ignorant of life-giving words and does not know the church’s rule",
          "issue": "Both negations are represented, but the scope of the first οὐκ across the coordinated description remains unresolved. The draft treats the entire described man as the excluded recipient of the chair. Its source_issues disclose this interpretation without establishing it. The period after κανόνα is an editorial feature of the supplied print, not independent evidence resolving the negation's scope.",
          "suggested_revision": "Provide separate syntactic evidence supporting the scope of the first οὐκ and its relationship to the explicitly negated εἰδώς. Preserve both negations and the supplied punctuation in the source record. Retain the unresolved meaning issue rather than harmonizing the passage into an unqualified assertion of the successor's learning.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "20",
      "verdict": "blocked",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
